## 4. Key Concepts Summary

| Concept              | What It Means                                              |
|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| **PE Format**        | Binary container format for all Windows executables        |
| **ImageBase**        | Preferred virtual address to load at (0x00400000 for exe)  |
| **RVA**              | Relative Virtual Address - offset from ImageBase           |
| **Import Table**     | List of DLLs and functions the exe needs                   |
| **IAT**              | Array of function pointers, filled in at load time         |
| **Export Table**     | Functions a DLL makes available to others                  |
| **Base Relocation**  | Fixup table for when DLL loads at non-preferred address    |
| **Section**          | Named block with specific memory permissions               |
| **Entry Point**      | First instruction to execute (CRT startup, not main)       |
| **Demand Paging**    | Pages loaded from disk only when first accessed            |

